<article class="env-proposition" id="35DC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/35DC">Proposition <span data-tag="35DC">6.5.1.18</span>.</a> Let $f: X \rightarrow Y$ be a morphism in an $\infty $-topos $\calX $, $\delta : X \rightarrow X \times _{Y} X$ the associated diagonal morphism, and $n \geq 0$. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The morphism $f$ is $n$-connective. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
The diagonal map $\delta : X \rightarrow X \times _{Y} X$ is $(n-1)$-connective, and $f$ is an effective epimorphism. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from Definition <a href="/tag/BAA1" data-tag="BAA1">6.5.1.10</a> and Remark <a href="/tag/8EA1" data-tag="8EA1">6.5.1.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>